ifcopenshell 0.8.0 vs boost 1.91: profile_point aggregate initializers.

Boost 1.91 switched boost::optional to the "union" implementation, whose
perfect-forwarding value constructor `optional(U&&)` is `explicit`. The
profile-definition mappings build `profile_point { std::array<double,2> xy;
boost::optional<double> radius; }` with `{{x,y},{f}}`, and the inner `{f}` is
copy-list-initialization, where an explicit constructor being selected is
ill-formed (GCC: "converting to 'boost::optional<double>' from initializer
list would use explicit constructor"). Plain copy-initialization from the
double (`{{x,y},f}`) never considers the explicit overload and picks the
non-explicit `optional(const T&)`, so this is a pure syntax change: same
value, same semantics, compiles on boost <= 1.89 too.

nixpkgs issue: https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/issues/562782
Generated 2026-09-13 with
  sed -E 's/\},[[:space:]]*\{[[:space:]]*([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*)[[:space:]]*\}[[:space:]]*\}/},\1}/g'
over the eight src/ifcgeom/mapping/*ProfileDef.cpp files that use the pattern
(45 sites). Not yet upstream (IfcOpenShell master carries the same code).

